<title>JAPAN: Tokyo Feb consumer prices rise 0.1 pct year/year.</title>
<headline>Tokyo Feb consumer prices rise 0.1 pct year/year.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tokyo area consumer prices rose 0.1 percent in February from a year earlier, while nationwide consumer prices for January increased 0.6 percent from a year earlier, the government's Management and Coordination Agency said on Friday.  </p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of consumer prices in Tokyo and nationwide (index base 1995):</p>
<p>					FEB	JAN	DEC</p>
<p> Tokyo overall index	    99.8     99.8     99.9</p>
<p>  yr-on-yr changes		+0.1pct   0.0pct  +0.2pct</p>
<p>  mth-on-mth changes	     0.0pct  -0.1pct  +0.1pct</p>
<p> Tokyo core index		 99.8     99.8     100.0</p>
<p>  yr-on-yr changes		+0.1pct  +0.1pct  -0.1pct</p>
<p>  mth-on-mth changes	     0.0pct  -0.2pct  -0.1pct</p>
<p>					JAN	DEC	NOV</p>
<p> Nationwide overall index     100.3    100.4    100.3</p>
<p>  yr-on-yr changes		 +0.6pct  +0.6pct  +0.5pct</p>
<p>  mth-on-mth changes	     -0.1pct  +0.1pct  -0.3pct</p>
<p> Nationwide core index	  100.1    100.5    100.6</p>
<p>  yr-on-yr changes		 +0.5pct  +0.3pct  +0.4pct</p>
<p>  mth-on-mth changes	     -0.4pct  -0.1pct  +0.1pct</p>
<p>(Note: The Tokyo index is calculated by collecting price data at mid-month. The core index, which is a key barometer for gauging core inflation, is overall prices minus fresh food prices. The base year has been changed to 1995 from 1990.)</p>
</text>
